{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788578965932651818,"compiled_state":{"alias":"bairnish-sunbeamed-nandine","assignee":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":8,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"936788dddd764d314f5719650a321bc248ba5b7380b67fb09b9d20b240dea4a4","event_uuid":"c193a0f7-25b5-497a-af0b-6b458a5476ef","position":{"commit_sha":"14f73ee9652914848a18ec56c089366a8270c1f6","position":"1788573178240474001-c193a0f7-25b5-497a-af0b-6b458a5476ef"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2e225d746f83ab5a959485b895e5a30fac850b89951896eaa5d73c9a866206ea","event_uuid":"c5f89acf-9935-4762-837f-938cad69b39d","position":{"commit_sha":"110bc3524368e0d6a3174cfb54707a4d8736f3f4","position":"1788573739033878578-c5f89acf-9935-4762-837f-938cad69b39d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9e9c54c2daea42c57123c50eba74f38ed846897d0a7600c30237c2e7fceee368","event_uuid":"0749d268-c6c1-452d-b1b4-235f97a7928e","position":{"commit_sha":"b9cbf216229d96126a1bd199aab88ae0c60869c8","position":"1788573837745710181-0749d268-c6c1-452d-b1b4-235f97a7928e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"17e9f909f33577ee343ea4b01534f4d1553c4ad71c8b51f74f9a0fc1cd85ff5a","event_uuid":"0cbee62d-d0c4-460d-abb4-76a98ec11a67","position":{"commit_sha":"f0cab11afc7febb0816c3b81e6e943e2a2a14f6a","position":"1788574061580248266-0cbee62d-d0c4-460d-abb4-76a98ec11a67"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ed9d391e3b0559cffaecbdd6001f9382bf877de5386b33b6f28e958475d25857","event_uuid":"4b63aed0-4950-47b7-99ab-51d90043ce92","position":{"commit_sha":"f0cab11afc7febb0816c3b81e6e943e2a2a14f6a","position":"1788574061660973932-4b63aed0-4950-47b7-99ab-51d90043ce92"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"b6530ab05a616803cb6e2c52130159c25d8eac958ffcc12fbb092abd504fe8de","event_uuid":"b9983e30-cbeb-47d2-ad44-f16c60123f3d","position":{"commit_sha":"c3dfdf61b5aaf30f5b5f2607bc15beae3a98dcd2","position":"1788575192783782367-b9983e30-cbeb-47d2-ad44-f16c60123f3d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"2f1421b2a05b334b4f4058d4f3a01d3798671461c644d6d751c966b864f9a076","event_uuid":"241c6042-6915-447b-8a89-b0a5ad00763b","position":{"commit_sha":"c22a77d058acf71820291f1646bfe6732b75c791","position":"1788578469416107275-241c6042-6915-447b-8a89-b0a5ad00763b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a302d6478ca0101fb1e4880822cffed78830f18f6ca9c7af27962a9dcd45cee7","event_uuid":"b74696da-b7f3-4d95-9966-0d9be07d125a","position":{"commit_sha":"51bf96d19c0325929797433f5de00d6068fe1484","position":"1788578965932651817-b74696da-b7f3-4d95-9966-0d9be07d125a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## AC1 — MEASURED live counts (growth vs. widening: GROWTH, widening REFUTED)\n\nMeasured 2026-09-05 against the live REB project (`https://navasage.atlassian.net`) with\nread-only `POST /rest/api/3/search/approximate-count`. No bridge write, no mutation.\n\n| Query | 2026-05-26 baseline | 2026-09-05 measured | Delta |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `project = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\"` (active) | 1,050 | **1,388** | +338 (+32%) |\n| `project = REB AND statusCategory = \"Done\"` (done) | 1,120 | **2,992** | +1,872 (+167%) |\n| `project = REB` (total) | 2,170 | **4,380** | +2,210 (+102%) |\n\nActive is 1,388 against a 1,200 ceiling: the active query is over by 188. That is the failing\nquery. The Done query cannot be the trigger — `_iter_pages` clips it at `_DONE_RECENT_CAP=1000`\n(the cap branch returns before cumulative could reach 1,200), so its 2,992 matches are already\nbeing reduced to the most-recent 1,000 by design.\n\n### Widening is REFUTED, three independent ways\n\n1. **Direct A/B of the old and new JQL against live data.** The only change to the query text\n   since the baseline probe was `status != \"Done\"` -> `statusCategory != \"Done\"`\n   (`3e5c7d39feaa`, 2026-08-15, ticket 7332). Both forms measured today:\n   - `project = REB AND status != \"Done\"` -> **1,388**\n   - `project = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\"` -> **1,388**\n\n   Identical. The switch matched zero additional issues.\n2. **REB's status set makes it a no-op.** REB exposes exactly `To Do`/`IDEA` (To Do),\n   `In Progress`/`In Review`/`Blocked` (In Progress), `Done` (Done). No Closed/Resolved/Cancelled,\n   so there is nothing for `statusCategory` to reclassify. If anything the switch could only\n   *narrow* active, never widen it.\n3. **Timing.** The statusCategory change landed 2026-08-15 and was followed by three weeks of\n   green hourly runs, including the eleven immediately before the failure. `git log` shows no\n   commit touching `jql_active` / `jql_done_recent` / `_ACLI_CEILING` between the last success\n   (00:59) and the first failure (01:33) — the JQL text has been byte-identical since 08-15.\n\n**Verdict: organic growth.** The active working set grew 1,050 -> 1,388 in ~14 weeks and crossed\nthe 1,200 ceiling. Nothing widened. This confirms the ticket's framing: the ceiling is a vendor\nlimit, the working set only grows, and the defect is that reconciliation capacity is coupled to\ntotal project size.\n\n## A second finding: `issuekey`-range partitioning is a SILENT-DROP TRAP — rejected\n\nKey-range slicing (`issuekey >= REB-a AND issuekey < REB-b`) was the first partition candidate:\nkeys are dense and monotonic, so a window of width W bounds the slice at W issues regardless of\nproject size. Measured against live Jira before adopting it, and it fails exactly the way this\nticket warns about:\n\n```\nproject = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\" AND issuekey < REB-5373   ->  1387   (REB-5373 exists)\nproject = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\" AND issuekey < REB-5501   ->     0   (REB-5501 does NOT exist)\nproject = REB AND statusCategory != \"Done\" AND issuekey < REB-9999   ->     0   (does NOT exist)\n```\n\nA relational `issuekey` comparison whose **boundary key does not exist** matches nothing, and\nreturns **no error**. Max key is REB-5373 while `project = REB` holds 4,380 issues, so ~1,000 key\nslots are gaps (deleted/moved issues) — any window whose boundary lands in a gap silently\ncontributes zero. A naive 500-wide tiling over REB-1..REB-5500 summed to **979** against a true\n1,388: **409 issues silently lost, raising nothing.** That is this bug wearing a new hat, and it\nwould have been invisible without measuring coverage.\n\n## Chosen partition key: `created` half-open windows\n\n`created` was validated the same way — an 8-window half-open tiling summed **exactly** to the\nwhole space:\n\n```\n[1970-01-01, 2026-01-01) 0    [2026-01-01, 2026-04-01) 0    [2026-04-01, 2026-06-01) 0\n[2026-06-01, 2026-07-01) 6    [2026-07-01, 2026-08-01) 61   [2026-08-01, 2026-08-15) 20\n[2026-08-15, 2026-09-01) 446  [2026-09-01, 2030-01-01) 855\nsum = 1388   whole-space = 1388\n```\n\nTwo properties decide it over the alternatives:\n\n- **Totality does not depend on a value existing.** `created < X` / `created >= X` partition the\n  space for *any* X, real issue or not — the exact property `issuekey` lacks.\n- **`created` is immutable.** `updated` changes under a running pass, so an issue touched\n  mid-scan can migrate between windows and be missed (or double-counted). `created` never moves,\n  so the windows are stable for the whole pass.\n\nDesign and seam guarantees to follow in the implementation comment.","timestamp":1788573739033878578},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Implementation — `collect_partitioned` in `fetch_paging.py`\n\n`_ACLI_CEILING` stays at **1200** and `_iter_pages` is **byte-unchanged**. The fix is a new\ndrain that runs *around* the pager, not through it.\n\n### Shape\n\n`drain(client, jql, page_size, cap)` routes one base query by its shape:\n\n- **`cap is None`** — the exhaustive active query. Goes to `collect_partitioned`.\n- **`cap is not None`** — the `ORDER BY updated DESC` done-recent query. Stays on the\n  single-query path. Partitioning a top-N read would silently change *which* issues it\n  selects, so `collect_partitioned` **refuses an `ORDER BY` query with a `ValueError`**\n  rather than mis-slicing it. (It also cannot reach the ceiling: the cap returns at 1,000.)\n\n`collect_partitioned` begins as the **single unbounded query** — byte-identical to what runs\ntoday — and only subdivides a window that *actually* raises the ceiling. A project under the\nceiling issues exactly the one query it always did; nothing changes until it has to.\n\nOn `SilentTruncationError(reason=\"ceiling\")` it replaces window `[lo, hi)` with `[lo, mid)`\nand `[mid, hi)` and re-asks. Windows are drained left to right off a LIFO, so the union comes\nback in `created` order.\n\n### Why it cannot silently drop a slice\n\n1. **The split is structurally exhaustive.** `[lo, mid) + [mid, hi)` covers exactly `[lo, hi)`\n   with no gap and no overlap **for any `mid`**. Coverage does not depend on choosing `mid`\n   well — only the probe count does. There is no arithmetic that can be off by one, because\n   the same `mid` value is the upper bound of one window and the lower bound of the next.\n2. **No sentinel dates.** The leftmost window omits `created >=` entirely and the rightmost\n   omits `created <`, so the outer edges stay genuinely unbounded. Nothing assumes a project\n   start date, and issues created *while the pass runs* still fall in the last window.\n3. **The partition key is immutable.** `created` never changes, so no issue migrates across a\n   boundary mid-pass. `updated` would have exactly that flaw.\n4. **The boundary need not exist.** This is what killed `issuekey` (see the measurement\n   comment): `created < X` and `created >= X` are complementary for any instant X.\n5. **Only the ceiling is ever intercepted.** `same-token-twice` and `offset-stall` propagate\n   out of any slice and abort the whole fetch — they are not retried as bisections, because a\n   stalled slice is untrustworthy, not merely too big.\n6. **The guard is preserved, not weakened.** When a window is already at Jira's finest\n   expressible resolution (one minute) the ceiling is **re-raised**. This path never returns a\n   partial slice; it only replaces one over-large *complete* read with several smaller\n   *complete* reads.\n\n### A new defence the tests forced out: the window-blind server\n\nRunning the existing suite surfaced a real hole. A client that **ignores the `created`\npredicate** (returns the full set for every window) can never be narrowed into compliance, so\nthe walk-back doubled its span until Python's date arithmetic threw `OverflowError` — an\nunhandled crash, and ~16 futile full drains first. This is the window-level sibling of the\nexisting offset-stall check (server ignoring `startAt`).\n\nFixed with `_MAX_SPAN` (40 years): past any plausible project history, the drain stops and\nre-raises the **ceiling**, loudly, after 11 probes instead of 16-plus-a-crash. That also fixed\na pre-existing test (`test_fetch_at_1200_issue_ceiling_raises_silent_truncation_error`) whose\nstub is exactly such a client.\n\n### Mutation results — 10/10 killed\n\nEach mutation was applied to `fetch_paging.py` in isolation and reverted after:\n\n| Mutation | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| drop the right slice | CAUGHT |\n| drop the left slice | CAUGHT |\n| gap at the seam (right child starts one minute late) | CAUGHT |\n| overlapping union (left child keeps the full upper bound) | CAUGHT |\n| half-open window becomes closed (`created <=`) | CAUGHT |\n| lower bound becomes exclusive (`created >`) | CAUGHT |\n| swallow every truncation reason, not just the ceiling | CAUGHT |\n| return a partial when the window cannot be split | CAUGHT |\n| drop the window-blind (`_MAX_SPAN`) guard | CAUGHT |\n| route the capped top-N query through the partitioner too | CAUGHT |\n\nTwo of these **survived the first round** and drove real test work rather than being written\nup as passes:\n\n- *gap at the seam* survived because the fixture's 17-minute issue spacing meant a one-minute\n  hole rarely landed on an issue. Closed two ways: a **structural** assertion that the\n  windows which actually completed chain end-to-end (first unbounded below, last unbounded\n  above, every `hi` equal to the next `lo`) — which catches a gap regardless of data density —\n  and a dense fixture at one issue per minute so every seam lands on a populated minute.\n- *drop the `_MAX_SPAN` guard* survived because the `OverflowError` fallback still produced\n  the right verdict, just slowly. Closed by asserting the probe budget (measured: 11 with the\n  guard, 16 without).\n\nThe `swallow every truncation reason` mutant is worth calling out: it makes\n`test_offset_stall_in_a_later_slice_still_raises` report **DID NOT RAISE** — i.e. that mutant\nreturns a silent partial snapshot. That is this bug's exact failure mode, and the seam tests\ncatch it.\n\n### Cost\n\nAgainst the measured REB shape (1,388 active) the drain settles at roughly six windows, four\nof which are ceiling probes — about 100 ACLI calls where today's (failing) query makes 14.\nThe pass already runs ~20 minutes dominated by enrichment, so this is not material, and the\nprobe count is logarithmic rather than proportional to project size. Noting it rather than\nhiding it.\n\n### Files\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetch_paging.py` — `collect_partitioned`, `drain`,\n  `_window_jql`, `_split_window` (190 -> 391 lines; cap is 800).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py` — `_fetch_project` calls `drain`. The\n  routing policy moved into `fetch_paging` specifically so this file stays at **650** lines,\n  the explicit target `test_fetch_paging_split.py` asserts (it went to 667 first).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_partitioned_fetch.py` — 17 tests.\n\n### AC status\n\n- **AC1** measured and recorded — growth, widening refuted (previous comment).\n- **AC2** `rebar bridge run` against live REB — **NOT verified by me.** Running the reconciler\n  live is a bridge *write* against a third-party system and is the operator's call. Verified\n  by proxy at the measured working-set size in `test_fetch_project_drains_the_measured_working_set_completely`.\n- **AC3** `_ACLI_CEILING` unchanged at 1200, with a regression test asserting it.\n- **AC4** demonstrated at 1,388 / 3,000 / 5,000 issues against a 1,200 ceiling.\n- **AC5** all three defences proven in a LATER slice, plus the new window-blind defence.\n- **AC6** workflow returns to green — pending merge; not verifiable pre-landing.","timestamp":1788575192783782367},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Pushed for review — Gerrit change 2657\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2657 — \"Partition the inbound fetch by created\nwindow\" (`af6fbfed9f8f`, 3 files, +527/-2).\n\nTicket left `in_progress` and the change left unsubmitted, per instruction: the operator\nverifies the votes and submits.\n\n### Gates run locally before push\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `make lint` (ruff check + format-check, zizmor, actionlint) | pass |\n| `make typecheck` (mypy, 762 source files) | pass |\n| complexity ratchet | `active=33 new=0 increased=0 stale=16` |\n| mechanism-delta ratchet | `active=684 new=0 increased=0 stale=0` |\n| `make verify` (full suite) | **19,449 passed, 72 skipped, 1 failed** in 50:21 |\n| module size | `fetch_paging.py` 391, `fetcher.py` 650 (cap 800; 650 is the explicit target `test_fetch_paging_split.py` asserts) |\n\n### The one failure, reported not papered over\n\n`tests/unit/test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation.py::test_verify_completion_partitions_attempt_without_changing_verdict`\nfailed with `GateCongestedError: gate admission refused: all 4 concurrent slots busy`, then\n**passed in isolation** (`7 passed in 97.62s`). It is a unit test coupled to a host-wide gate\nadmission semaphore, contended by the other agent sessions running on this box. Zero overlap\nwith this change (the file contains no reference to `fetch_paging`, `fetcher`,\n`collect_partitioned` or `_ACLI_CEILING`).\n\nFiled as `torrential-unwhite-snail` (`9c2e-b44c-119e-4105`), linked `discovered_from` this\nticket, rather than retried into green.\n\n### No gate refusals\n\n`claim` succeeded without a plan-review block, and no `--force` or bypass was used on any\nsurface at any point.\n\n### What was NOT done, deliberately\n\n- **No live `rebar bridge run`** (AC2). Running the reconciler against live Jira is a bridge\n  write to a third-party system and the operator's call. Only read-only\n  `POST /rest/api/3/search/approximate-count` and `GET .../search/jql` calls were made, for the\n  measurements above.\n- **Change not submitted, ticket not closed.**","timestamp":1788578469416107275}],"created_at":1788573178240474001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b74696da-b7f3-4d95-9966-0d9be07d125a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cb2b-6fb5-226b-457d"}],"description":"## The failure\n\nThe scheduled **Reconcile Bridge** workflow began failing at 2026-09-05T01:33 UTC after\n**eleven consecutive successes** (hourly, 14:28 through 00:59). It will now fail every hour\nuntil fixed; Jira/rebar divergence accumulates silently in the meantime.\n\nRun `33936533951`, job \"Run rebar reconciler\":\n\n```\nERROR: reconcile_once raised: ACLI working set reached the 1200-issue ceiling\n       (JRACLOUD-94632 silent truncation)\nReconcile failed (exit 1)\n```\n\n## Where it comes from\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetch_paging.py`\n\n- `:25` — `_ACLI_CEILING = 1200`\n- the ceiling branch in `_iter_pages` — `if accumulated + len(page) >= _ACLI_CEILING: raise\n  SilentTruncationError(..., reason=\"ceiling\")`\n\n**The guard is behaving correctly and should not be weakened.** It refuses to hand back a\nsilently-truncated snapshot, which would feed `_build_snapshot` and make whole issues invisible\nto the pass rather than merely under-populated. A loud hourly failure is strictly better than a\nquiet partial reconcile. This ticket is not \"the guard is too strict\".\n\n## Why raising the constant is the WRONG fix\n\nThe constant already carries its own history, verbatim from `:19-24`:\n\n```\n# Hard ACLI per-query ceiling. Raised from 1,000 to 1,200 in bug f6cc\n# after empirical confirmation that the DIG working set has 1,050 active\n# issues + 1,120 Done issues (probe 2026-05-26). 1,200 covers active\n# with ~150-issue headroom and bounds the Done query under its 1,000-\n# issue cap (see _DONE_RECENT_CAP).\n```\n\nThis is the SECOND time the ceiling has been reached. It was raised 1,000 -> 1,200 with roughly\n150 issues of headroom; that headroom is now gone. Raising it to 1,400 buys another few months\nand guarantees a third occurrence, because the ceiling is a **vendor limit** (JRACLOUD-94632) and\nthe working set only grows. The defect is not the number. It is that reconciliation capacity is\ncoupled to total project size, when it need not be.\n\nThe fix direction is **partition the query** so no single ACLI call approaches the ceiling —\nslice by status, by updated-date window, or by key range, and union the results — making capacity\nindependent of how large REB grows. Whatever partition is chosen must preserve the existing\nanti-truncation guarantees: the cursor-stall, offset-stall and short-page defences in\n`_iter_pages` exist because each one was a real silent-partial bug, and a partitioned fetch must\nnot reintroduce them at the seam between slices.\n\n## Confirm before fixing (do not assume)\n\nThe obvious story is \"the working set grew past the headroom\". That is an INFERENCE, not a\nmeasurement, and there is a competing explanation that would call for a different fix: the JQL\ncould have WIDENED, so the same project now matches more issues. Measure the current matched\ncount per query and compare against the 2026-05-26 probe (1,050 active / 1,120 Done) before\nchoosing a design. If the query widened, narrowing it may be the correct and much smaller fix.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The current matched-issue count for each reconciler query is MEASURED and recorded on this\n      ticket, alongside the 2026-05-26 baseline, establishing growth vs. query-widening as cause.\n- [ ] `rebar bridge run` completes against the live REB project without raising\n      `SilentTruncationError(reason=\"ceiling\")`.\n- [ ] `_ACLI_CEILING` is NOT raised as the fix. (Removing the need for a large ceiling is in\n      scope; weakening the guard is not.)\n- [ ] Reconciliation capacity no longer scales with total project size — demonstrated by a test\n      that drives the fetch path with a working set materially LARGER than the ceiling and\n      asserts a complete, non-truncated snapshot.\n- [ ] The existing anti-truncation guarantees still hold across the new partition seam:\n      cursor-stall (\"same-token-twice\"), offset-stall (server ignoring `startAt`), and the\n      short-page-is-not-exhaustion rule each still raise or continue as they do today, proven by\n      tests at the seam between slices, not only within one slice.\n- [ ] The Reconcile Bridge workflow returns to green on its hourly schedule.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetch_paging.py","reason":"Add created-window partitioned drain (recursive bisection on the ceiling signal); _iter_pages and _ACLI_CEILING unchanged."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"Route the uncapped active base query through the partitioned drain; the capped ORDER BY done query stays on the single-query path."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/fetch/test_fetcher_partitioned_fetch.py","reason":"New: working set materially larger than the ceiling returns a complete snapshot; cursor-stall/offset-stall/short-page defences proven AT the partition seam; window tiling coverage/disjointness."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","cb2b-6fb5-226b-457d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"0cbee62d-d0c4-460d-abb4-76a98ec11a67","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5c5c-5741-9b33-47fa","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconcile Bridge is down: ACLI 1200-issue ceiling reached, hourly Jira sync failing since 01:33 -- second time this ceiling has been hit, so raising the constant is not the fix","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c193a0f7-25b5-497a-af0b-6b458a5476ef","c5f89acf-9935-4762-837f-938cad69b39d","0749d268-c6c1-452d-b1b4-235f97a7928e","0cbee62d-d0c4-460d-abb4-76a98ec11a67","4b63aed0-4950-47b7-99ab-51d90043ce92","b9983e30-cbeb-47d2-ad44-f16c60123f3d","241c6042-6915-447b-8a89-b0a5ad00763b","b74696da-b7f3-4d95-9966-0d9be07d125a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788578965932651818,"uuid":"c272bc3f-86f5-49f3-a49e-edef01209fc2"}